1
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,420
No!

2
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,910
My name is Kudo Shinichi.

3
00:01:38,290 --> 00:01:41,580
I was a famous high school
student detective.

4
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:47,090
But one day, I went with my childhood
friend Ran to an amusement park and ...

5
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:51,410
...I witnessed a scene of some men in
black involved in some suspicious deal.

6
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:56,050
And then they made me take
a poison known as Apoptoxin 4869.

7
00:01:56,050 --> 00:01:57,440
When I woke up...

8
00:01:57,890 --> 00:01:59,890
..my body had been shrunken.

9
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:01,950
If they knew that Kudo Shinichi was still alive...

10
00:02:02,050 --> 00:02:06,050
...the Black Organization could
bring harm to all those around me.

11
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:08,060
Naming myself Edogawa Conan...

12
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:11,950
...I solved cases while looking
for information on those men.

13
00:02:12,450 --> 00:02:17,520
But this is a case that occurred 100
days before I became Edogawa Conan.

14
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:23,060
While taking a trip with Ran and others,
we came across the village's legend...

15
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:25,890
..and became involved in an
impossible murder case.

16
00:02:26,770 --> 00:02:28,690
A series of mysteries occurred...

17
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:32,570
...and I, too, suffered
an unexpected trick.

18
00:02:40,030 --> 00:02:41,030
Wait.

19
00:02:42,050 --> 00:02:44,580
A rumor about the high school student
who's a great detective has appeared.

20
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,050
You've solved a murder case
once again, haven't you?

21
00:02:47,050 --> 00:02:50,260
This time, it was a closed room case,
how did you figure out the murderer?

22
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,140
You were brilliant this time too, weren't you?

23
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:53,310
How did you feel when
the police detectives...

24
00:02:53,350 --> 00:02:55,460
...found themselves in over
their heads as you solved it?

25
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:00,700
Ah, let's see...

26
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:03,660
Yes, this is me.

27
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:06,740
The high school student
detective, Kudo Shinichi.

28
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:10,720
Of course at the time I couldn't have
imagined that, in the near future...

29
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:12,940
...I would be reverting back to being
an elementary school student.

30
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:15,900
Well, how do I put it...

31
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:18,080
- Kudo.
- One word, please.

32
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:20,080
Oi!

33
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:23,460
Ha!

34
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,880
That was dangerous!

35
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,020
She's Mori Ran.

36
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:33,020
My childhood friend.

37
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:38,040
Deep down a good girl, but she's also
strong willed and gifted in karate.

38
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:41,560
We aren't dating though.

39
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:45,460
Anyway, let’s run, let’s run!

40
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:54,800
Itadakimasu!

41
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:58,340
Please don't hold back and
eat as much as you like.

42
00:03:58,630 --> 00:04:03,060
Ran has been so worried about her 
figure, that she hasn't been eating at all.

43
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:05,620
I am discouraged, you know.

44
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,620
Mom, that's not true.

45
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:10,120
Thank you very much.
I'll eat heartily.

46
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:12,120
Yeah, go ahead.

47
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:16,360
Well? Any good?

48
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:17,920
"It's bad!"

49
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:20,920
Lately...I've also been
worried about my figure.

50
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:24,840
It itches. Ah!

51
00:04:24,910 --> 00:04:26,300
Mom, what's the matter?

52
00:04:26,460 --> 00:04:31,160
Recently, when someone lies,
my left eye starts to itch.

53
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,460
Eh?

54
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:38,140
Well, I run into so many
incidents of it as a lawyer...

55
00:04:38,290 --> 00:04:42,050
...but it troubles me most
when my clients start lying.

56
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:45,470
Because of that, my eye's
gotten very sensitive to lies.

57
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:48,780
It's my predisposition
towards cause and effect.

58
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:52,480
Ah, it's kind of an occupational disease.

59
00:04:53,070 --> 00:04:54,870
This person is Kisaki Eri.

60
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:58,740
She's a shrewd lawyer who never
loses a case and she's Ran's mother.

61
00:04:58,820 --> 00:05:02,690
However she and Ran's father,
Mori Kogoro, live separately...

62
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,580
...and are negotiating their divorce.

63
00:05:04,830 --> 00:05:09,000
And? Shinichi, what
was that lie just now?

64
00:05:09,470 --> 00:05:11,980
Eh? "Bad cook"

65
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:14,900
Ah, Mom, a visitor.

66
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:17,480
Eh? Who could that be?

67
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:25,580
Sonoko!

68
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:27,580
Ran, I'm here.

69
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:31,420
Hello, Kudo. Popular
as ever, aren't you?

70
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:33,320
I saw you on TV.

71
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:36,600
<i>This stuff's awful! I don't want this.</i>

72
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:40,800
I'm not happy about it. 
I can't go home.

73
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:43,160
Then I'm just in time.

74
00:05:43,790 --> 00:05:47,980
Say, it's very sudden., but how about
we all go to Jyugoya Village?

75
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:50,420
This is Suzuki Sonoko.

76
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:52,540
The daughter of the Suzuki Conglomerate.

77
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:57,080
She's one of Japan's richest people, but
she's sociable and follows the latest trends.

78
00:05:57,200 --> 00:06:02,440
She's always inviting us to wherever
various incidents have occurred.

79
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:04,860
Jyugoya Village?

80
00:06:05,010 --> 00:06:08,600
Papa's acquaintance built a villa there
and he's invited me to come visit.

81
00:06:08,850 --> 00:06:11,720
Could it be this acquaintance
of your father's is...

82
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:13,240
Bingo!

83
00:06:13,310 --> 00:06:18,000
Japan's biggest chain of izakayas
that you're the legal adviser for...

84
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:21,110
Wakura Group’s President Wakura!

85
00:06:21,530 --> 00:06:24,560
Uncle Wakura said he really
wants you to come.

86
00:06:25,990 --> 00:06:31,020
If Wakura is asking...can't
turn him down, now can I?

87
00:06:31,110 --> 00:06:32,640
Yay!

88
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:33,940
Ah!

89
00:06:34,290 --> 00:06:34,980
Huh?

90
00:06:35,780 --> 00:06:36,980
What about Dad?

91
00:06:37,050 --> 00:06:38,600
I don't want that person going with us.

92
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:53,880
Rascal!

93
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:55,910
Rascal!

94
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,250
Ras...

95
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:59,860
Like I said, it's "Pascal."

96
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:01,860
That's so ambiguous...

97
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:04,740
Normally a raccoon's name is Rascal.

98
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:07,630
Mine is far more clever
than any 'Rascal' would be.

99
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:23,980
Oh?

100
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:32,680
Oh, I just heard something.

101
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,860
It might be Pascal! 
Please go take a look.

102
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:35,760
Eh?

103
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:37,800
You... want me to go up there?

104
00:07:37,870 --> 00:07:39,250
Eh? You won't go up?
"Acrophobia"

105
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:41,680
Then I won't pay you.

106
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:44,640
I came because you said
there was a kidnapping.

107
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:46,110
Why is this happening to me...

108
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:48,180
Ah, did you say something just now?

109
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:49,560
No, no, no.

110
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:52,760
Oh! There, Wait...

111
00:07:56,400 --> 00:08:00,800
By the way, this uncle is
Ran's father, Mori Kogoro.

112
00:08:00,890 --> 00:08:03,860
He left the police and
opened a detective agency...

113
00:08:03,930 --> 00:08:05,680
...but as for his ability...

114
00:08:05,750 --> 00:08:07,460
..well, how can I put this...

115
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:08,260
Pascal.

116
00:08:08,370 --> 00:08:13,060
Anyhow, we decided to leave him
behind and head to Jyugoya Village.

117
00:08:13,350 --> 00:08:15,840
Pascal!

118
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:20,240
"Northeast Bus Stop Jyugoya Village"

119
00:08:20,350 --> 00:08:22,960
We’re here at last....

120
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:26,380
But why are you still in
your school uniform?

121
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:29,220
No choice. I couldn't go home, after all.

122
00:08:30,610 --> 00:08:32,730
Uncle Wakura, it's been awhile!

123
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:35,370
Yes... Welcome.
"Wakura Group President Wakura Isami"

124
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,580
Hello.

125
00:08:36,650 --> 00:08:38,420
-It's been awhile.
-Yes it is.

126
00:08:40,300 --> 00:08:41,060
Who is this?

127
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:43,060
Ah, my daughter.

128
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,470
My close friend, Mori Ran...

129
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:48,140
...and the famous high school student
detective, Kudo Shinichi

130
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:49,010
Hello.

131
00:08:49,050 --> 00:08:49,850
Hello.

132
00:08:50,730 --> 00:08:51,680
A detective?

133
00:08:51,770 --> 00:08:55,200
Wakura, we're sorry for forcing
ourselves upon you like this today.

134
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:58,260
Not at all, not at all.
It's an honor to have you come.

135
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:02,220
Welcome to the village
of the legendary Otori.

136
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:04,780
"Village of the legendary Otori"?

137
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:08,000
In this village a long time ago...

138
00:09:08,410 --> 00:09:12,420
...legend has it that a huge Mozu
appeared, attacking the villagers...

139
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:15,020
...and making them what
is called a hayanie.

140
00:09:15,670 --> 00:09:17,020
Hayanie?

141
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:20,170
When a Mozu catches insects and frogs...

142
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,780
...and has the trait of impaling
them on tree branches.

143
00:09:22,850 --> 00:09:24,780
Those are the Mozu's prey.

144
00:09:24,850 --> 00:09:29,080
It's characteristic is to stick them on
sharp objects like barbed wire and twigs.

145
00:09:29,650 --> 00:09:31,540
Ah, there, there.

146
00:09:31,950 --> 00:09:33,300
There's one.

147
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:37,480
Eh? Auntie, that surprised me!

148
00:09:37,550 --> 00:09:40,560
Dad, don't shock them like that anymore.

149
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:43,410
I'm sorry... Nice to meet you.

150
00:09:43,470 --> 00:09:45,140
I'm his daughter Misa.
"Wakura's Second Daughter Wakura Misa"

151
00:09:45,190 --> 00:09:48,290
I'm helping Wakura
investigate the Otori legend.

152
00:09:48,350 --> 00:09:49,480
I'm Kosaka.
"Graduate Student Kosaka Sho"

153
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,150
We'll be under your care.

154
00:09:51,230 --> 00:09:53,670
I got caught up in the Otori
legend just now. Excuse me.

155
00:09:54,530 --> 00:09:55,800
Come, let's go.

156
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:56,550
Yes.

157
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,640
"Jyugoya Village"

158
00:10:16,010 --> 00:10:17,940
This is a nice place, isn't it?

159
00:10:18,420 --> 00:10:20,660
But, scary!

160
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:25,660
Still, the only access to the
village is across this bridge.

161
00:10:25,730 --> 00:10:27,540
So do your best for a little longer.

162
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,540
Yes!

163
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,220
Hey, Ran!

164
00:10:32,290 --> 00:10:33,220
Sorry!

165
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:35,620
Why are you wearing these shoes for?

166
00:10:35,670 --> 00:10:37,820
You should have brought some
that were more for walking.

167
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:40,540
You don't understand, Shinichi.

168
00:10:40,610 --> 00:10:44,040
She’s at an age when the emphasis is
more on appearance than practicality.

169
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:47,520
Appearance? Who's going to be
looking at you here in the mountains?

170
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:49,520
See, you totally don't get it.

171
00:10:49,950 --> 00:10:52,260
It's okay. I like this.

172
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:55,580
If you fall, you'll definitely die.

173
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:58,330
Hey! Hey there!

174
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:01,720
Shinichi, stop it! You're the worst!

175
00:11:01,810 --> 00:11:06,480
Stop it, you guys! That's dangerous!

176
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,640
It's slippery here. Be careful.

177
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:26,400
Because you're a guy, you go first.

178
00:11:26,460 --> 00:11:29,400
Don't push, that's dangerous.
All right, I'll go.

179
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:32,660
You are too strong despite being women.
"Mozutobi Shrine"

180
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:33,360
What?!

181
00:11:35,910 --> 00:11:38,490
Wow, great.

182
00:11:44,010 --> 00:11:47,720
What are the characteristics
of the village's Otori legend?

183
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:52,680
It's very similar to the legend recorded on
Forbina ruins from Mayan civilization.

184
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:57,790
Ever since my school days, I've been
chasing cases across the globe...

185
00:11:57,870 --> 00:12:00,800
...of Otori legend or legendary
monstrous birds.

186
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:02,500
This is a rare case.

187
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:07,130
There are these ruins in this village,
so there may be a possibility that...

188
00:12:07,220 --> 00:12:12,680
...they have been transmitted from
ancient Mayan civilization to Japan.

189
00:12:12,770 --> 00:12:14,420
It could be a great discovery.

190
00:12:16,650 --> 00:12:18,180
What is that?

191
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:28,260
People of the village call it, "God's Perch."
"Mozutobi Shrine God's Perch"

192
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:31,400
This was the place where sacrifices were made to Lord Otori.

193
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:33,400
Sacrifices?

194
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:36,460
Yes.

195
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:41,280
One would be chosen as a
hayanie and be sacrificed here.

196
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:44,160
It's said that Lord Otori's wrath would be quelled…

197
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:47,700
...and that famine and catastrophe
would hopefully not occur.

198
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:50,090
They can be found anywhere around the village.

199
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:54,460
Good afternoon.

200
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:56,840
Ah, good afternoon.

201
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:58,420
Ah, you have guests?

202
00:12:58,480 --> 00:12:59,380
Yes.

203
00:12:59,470 --> 00:13:01,380
It's great to have such fine weather.

204
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:03,740
What business do you have at the shrine, Mr. Policeman?

205
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:04,440
Yes.

206
00:13:04,590 --> 00:13:07,800
I was pressed into helping with
the preparations for the festival.

207
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:10,060
Uncle, is there a festival?

208
00:13:10,110 --> 00:13:11,360
3 days from now.

209
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:12,820
What kind of festival is it?

210
00:13:12,930 --> 00:13:17,120
Ah, here at the Mozutobi Shrine,
there's to be a festival to Lord Otori.

211
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:20,440
In order to calm Lord Otori's turbulent soul...

212
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:24,570
They'll be dressed as birds and
chant prayers while dancing.

213
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:27,560
But, for this year only,
this one will be special.

214
00:13:27,850 --> 00:13:28,780
Right, Mr. Policeman?

215
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:30,410
Ah, that's right. years

216
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:33,780
A bronze mirror, which is a national
treasure that can only be viewed ...

217
00:13:33,830 --> 00:13:35,760
...once every 300 years will be
here at the inner shrine.

218
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:39,860
The festival 3 days from now only
comes once every 300 years.

219
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,080
Are you serious?!

220
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:42,800
Once every 300 years?

221
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:45,000
We're super lucky, aren't we?

222
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:47,540
We get to see a hidden mirror
(hikyo) in an unexplored area. (hikyo)

223
00:13:47,650 --> 00:13:48,440
Eh?

224
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:49,910
Hikyo(coward)?

225
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:53,040
It means "secret mirror."

226
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:56,620
Don't make me explain my puns.

227
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:57,710
Sorry.

228
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:02,580
But, it really is a secret mirror.

229
00:14:03,570 --> 00:14:07,690
Legend has it that
mysterious things occur...

230
00:14:07,770 --> 00:14:10,560
...when the bronze mirror
resonates with the God's Perch.

231
00:14:10,650 --> 00:14:12,260
What mysterious things?

232
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:14,880
Ah, from reading the ancient literature...

233
00:14:14,970 --> 00:14:17,260
It’s something like a total solar eclipse.

234
00:14:17,810 --> 00:14:19,340
A total solar eclipse?

235
00:14:19,940 --> 00:14:25,280
But, I'm sure the next cycle
in Japan won't be until 2035.

236
00:14:25,590 --> 00:14:27,020
Ridiculous, isn't it?

237
00:14:28,330 --> 00:14:30,800
But, believers have their dreams.

238
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:36,460
Most of the people in the village
seem to get a little nervous,...

239
00:14:36,540 --> 00:14:38,930
...thinking of whether or
not they’ll be be cursed...

240
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:59,840
Since you have come,
please stay here for the festival.

241
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:47,430
Didn't you listen to what I just told you?

242
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:54,680
Dad!

243
00:15:57,340 --> 00:15:58,900
Dad, are you okay?
"Wakura's Eldest Son Wakura Yoichi"

244
00:16:00,140 --> 00:16:02,140
Say, what caused this to happen?
"Wakura's Eldest Daughter Wakura Kotomi"

245
00:16:02,910 --> 00:16:04,760
It's unbelievable.
"Wakura's Second Son Wakura Ryoji"

246
00:16:05,270 --> 00:16:10,180
While all of us were walking around
and chatting, then we heard a bird cry.

247
00:16:10,180 --> 00:16:11,960
And suddenly, Kosaka...

248
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:16,540
It's true! We then realized that
Kosaka had been stuck up there!

249
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:22,660
It's regrettable that I'm still safe.

250
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:25,140
What are you saying?

251
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:26,460
Dad!

252
00:16:28,410 --> 00:16:29,700
Dad.

253
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:31,860
What's the matter? Does it hurt?

254
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:34,060
Are you okay?

255
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:35,780
I'm fine.

256
00:16:35,780 --> 00:16:37,300
Wakura.

257
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:46,200
That truly is regrettable.

258
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:48,660
Brother Ryoji!

259
00:16:51,110 --> 00:16:52,500
Kudo!

260
00:16:54,810 --> 00:16:56,130
Kudo, isn't it?

261
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:59,060
This person is Megure Juzo.

262
00:16:59,450 --> 00:17:02,400
He's Ran's father's former boss.

263
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:05,600
He's called the 'Demon
Inspector of the MPD'...

264
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:08,300
...but in reality, he's also a devoted husband.

265
00:17:08,450 --> 00:17:10,780
What are you doing at a place like this for?

266
00:17:11,150 --> 00:17:14,300
I was invited by Sonoko to come
to a villa here in this village.

267
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:17,360
Inspector Megure, what are you doing here?

268
00:17:17,530 --> 00:17:21,520
Well, I came to attend a training at this
prefectural police and they said that...

269
00:17:21,670 --> 00:17:26,670
...a murder had taken place, so I came
to help out in the investigation.

270
00:17:27,370 --> 00:17:29,480
It’s Lord Otori's curse!

271
00:17:31,490 --> 00:17:34,730
He’s finally attacking people,
making them hayanie...

272
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:38,090
It's the legendary Otori becoming real!

273
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:41,890
In this once-every-300 years festival...

274
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:46,710
because of the Wakura family's
investigation and excavation of the ruins...

275
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:51,900
...and selfish behavior,
Lord Otori has been angered!

276
00:17:51,970 --> 00:17:53,800
It's as the storyteller says!

277
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:55,500
That's right, it's the curse!

278
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:59,060
The curse! The curse!

279
00:17:59,300 --> 00:18:02,260
Who's the old lady?

280
00:18:02,530 --> 00:18:04,920
She seems to be called "the storyteller."

281
00:18:05,050 --> 00:18:07,950
She must be the one who
manages the shrine here.

282
00:18:08,030 --> 00:18:11,000
Ah... This investigation will be difficult.

283
00:18:12,110 --> 00:18:13,800
Eh...

284
00:18:14,030 --> 00:18:19,620
In order to investigate the corpse,
he will be taken down to the village.

285
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:23,940
Because we'll be listening to the
circumstances of each of you in turn...

286
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:27,750
...none of you may leave the village.

287
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:32,870
And, since the crime
scene must be preserved...

288
00:18:32,930 --> 00:18:35,800
...please refrain from entering the shrine.

289
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:36,600
Yes!

290
00:18:38,290 --> 00:18:39,850
You are? Let's see...

291
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:42,100
Ah! Patrolman Haji at your service!

292
00:18:42,170 --> 00:18:44,220
I’m counting on you.

293
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:45,150
Yes sir!

294
00:19:10,250 --> 00:19:12,040
People can't die from a legend.

295
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:16,440
This is...a murder case.

296
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:21,350
This impossible murder mystery...

297
00:19:23,130 --> 00:19:24,520
I will solve it!

298
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:29,280
"Wakura Family Villa"

299
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:46,640
Well, well, well... sorry for being late.

300
00:19:47,450 --> 00:19:48,950
This voice is...

301
00:19:49,020 --> 00:19:53,240
<i>Oh, Bret Nelli, where is your house?</i>

302
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:58,720
Everybody, are you having fun?

303
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:00,060
Dad...

304
00:20:00,140 --> 00:20:02,900
Why is he here?

305
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:05,220
Oh, oh?

306
00:20:05,850 --> 00:20:10,840
The conversation doesn't seem
to be as lively as I had imagined.

307
00:20:10,890 --> 00:20:15,100
As I thought, you can't fill in the void
with the detective boy himself.

308
00:20:15,470 --> 00:20:20,640
When it comes to solving mysteries and
socializing, he still has a long way to go!

309
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:24,560
That man has bad timing.

310
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:31,460
I see...

311
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:34,660
This is a murder case.

312
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:37,700
Most regrettable.

313
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:42,720
If this detective, Mori Kogoro,
had came just a little earlier...

314
00:20:42,800 --> 00:20:45,300
I would have caught the
criminal just like that.

315
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:47,500
What are you saying?

316
00:20:47,550 --> 00:20:50,470
If the criminal was stupid enough
to be caught by you...

317
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:52,860
...Shinichi would have
caught him ages ago.

318
00:20:52,970 --> 00:20:55,620
The detective boy is my pupil.
I taught him everything.

319
00:20:55,690 --> 00:20:58,680
Ah, itchy, itchy!

320
00:21:01,570 --> 00:21:02,680
Here you are.

321
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:03,440
Thank you.

322
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:07,940
At any rate, your father seems
to be a huge bird lover.

323
00:21:08,430 --> 00:21:09,980
Birds, here, there and everywhere.

324
00:21:11,780 --> 00:21:15,140
My father is serious about
investigating the Otori legend.

325
00:21:15,470 --> 00:21:17,760
It's amazing how passionate he is…

326
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:19,910
...to the extent of buying up
all the land in the village.

327
00:21:23,290 --> 00:21:24,710
Excuse me.

328
00:21:34,540 --> 00:21:37,000
When you look closely...he’s hot.

329
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,300
Sonoko, it’s wrong at a time like this.

330
00:21:40,650 --> 00:21:44,740
Now that I, the great detective
Mori Kogoro have come...

331
00:21:44,810 --> 00:21:48,160
...this case is as good as solved.

332
00:21:48,450 --> 00:21:52,500
Please tell your father to be at ease.

333
00:21:52,580 --> 00:21:53,610
Ah, itchy!

334
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:57,040
If I could have an aperitif, my head
would become increasingly clearer.

335
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:59,070
Ah, so itchy!

336
00:22:28,940 --> 00:22:29,960
Oh, delicious!

337
00:22:31,040 --> 00:22:32,580
As way of saying thanks…

338
00:22:33,790 --> 00:22:39,700
I, the great detective Mori Kogoro,
will settle this incident perfectly.

339
00:22:40,850 --> 00:22:44,030
Truth is, I have already...

340
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:48,820
...figured out the criminal.

341
00:22:49,210 --> 00:22:50,480
Who is the criminal?

342
00:22:51,950 --> 00:22:53,580
The criminal is...

343
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:55,720
The criminal is?

344
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:57,460
The criminal is...

345
00:22:57,590 --> 00:22:59,490
The criminal is?

346
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:03,510
A human!

347
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:11,570
Everyone...the Otori legend
is just superstition.

348
00:23:12,010 --> 00:23:16,740
In this 21st century, for educated
adults to be misled by a superstition...

349
00:23:16,790 --> 00:23:17,850
...is absolutely disgraceful.

350
00:23:17,970 --> 00:23:18,670
Eh?

351
00:23:18,950 --> 00:23:20,080
Dad, that's all?

352
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:21,040
Yeah.

353
00:23:21,820 --> 00:23:26,140
Don't you have a concrete
idea about who the suspect is?

354
00:23:26,260 --> 00:23:27,270
Nope!

355
00:23:33,650 --> 00:23:34,830
Excuse me a minute.

356
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,820
The Otori legend, huh?

357
00:23:40,380 --> 00:23:45,020
Aren't such things told to protect
treasure from looters, in many cases?

358
00:23:48,560 --> 00:23:53,920
You’re saying that...there's real
treasure buried in this village?

359
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:58,680
It's just like looking for the
Tokugawa buried treasure, isn't it?

360
00:23:58,800 --> 00:24:00,680
The Tokugawa buried treasure!

361
00:24:01,280 --> 00:24:03,640
A man's romance!

362
00:24:04,690 --> 00:24:06,110
What man's romance?

363
00:24:06,580 --> 00:24:08,650
The Tokugawa buried treasure, huh?

364
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:11,540
How should I declare
it on my tax returns?

365
00:24:20,350 --> 00:24:23,080
There is also a romantic
legend in this village.

366
00:24:23,220 --> 00:24:25,840
Eh? What is it? Please tell us.

367
00:24:26,210 --> 00:24:30,270
That lovers who exchange kisses
beneath the God's Perch...

368
00:24:33,800 --> 00:24:35,520
...will never be parted and be married for life.

369
00:24:35,580 --> 00:24:36,950
Kiss...

370
00:24:39,270 --> 00:24:42,420
It's a legend only girls would believe in.

371
00:24:43,020 --> 00:24:46,460
Ran, wants to give it a test!

372
00:24:48,500 --> 00:24:49,770
I won't do that!

373
00:24:51,590 --> 00:24:55,850
Something called Otori that has attacked
village people and made them its hayanie.

374
00:24:57,140 --> 00:25:00,270
And a legend of a kiss in this village.

375
00:25:01,690 --> 00:25:03,900
That's a great mismatch here.

376
00:25:05,960 --> 00:25:09,640
I found this up at the scene just now.

377
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:15,780
These carvings. I wonder
if they're characters?

378
00:25:15,920 --> 00:25:18,540
They're similar to the characters
used at the Fobina ruins.

379
00:25:19,340 --> 00:25:21,980
If I'm certain, this means "curse."

380
00:25:22,410 --> 00:25:23,830
"Curse"?

381
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:28,760
Would you know what this fragment is?

382
00:25:42,040 --> 00:25:43,040
Dad?

383
00:25:46,030 --> 00:25:47,500
Dad?!

384
00:25:49,270 --> 00:25:52,920
Wakura?! Wakura! Are you okay?

385
00:25:53,920 --> 00:25:55,540
What is this?

386
00:25:55,540 --> 00:25:57,540
What's going on?

387
00:25:57,580 --> 00:25:58,880
What's happening?

388
00:26:00,380 --> 00:26:01,710
What is this?

389
00:26:09,320 --> 00:26:10,810
Shinichi!

390
00:26:11,140 --> 00:26:12,710
Dad! Are you alright?

391
00:26:12,890 --> 00:26:14,550
Wakura! Wakura!

392
00:26:15,020 --> 00:26:16,860
Uncle, are you okay?

393
00:26:16,930 --> 00:26:18,480
Dad, hang in there.

394
00:26:36,890 --> 00:26:37,720
Damn!

395
00:26:59,180 --> 00:27:00,650
How did it go?

396
00:27:03,020 --> 00:27:04,420
This just struck so suddenly.

397
00:27:05,340 --> 00:27:06,900
What on earth happened?!

398
00:27:07,900 --> 00:27:09,840
Oh? Where's Wakura?

399
00:27:09,840 --> 00:27:12,690
Why are you getting so
worked up over a blackout?

400
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:14,640
Well, it wasn't about that!

401
00:27:14,760 --> 00:27:17,240
A bird-man suddenly came and...

402
00:27:17,420 --> 00:27:18,460
Yoichi.

403
00:27:18,560 --> 00:27:22,740
Your father had a spasm and Ryoji and the others attended him back to his room.

404
00:27:22,860 --> 00:27:23,860
My father?

405
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:26,420
His room...?
Didn't you call an ambulance?

406
00:27:26,740 --> 00:27:29,520
-Well that's...
-An ambulance would be overkill.

407
00:27:29,780 --> 00:27:32,740
Having him examined by some
country hospital would be pointless.

408
00:27:33,220 --> 00:27:35,040
If his condition's still bad in the morning...

409
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:37,520
...we'll take him to Tokyo
to be examined there.

410
00:27:37,700 --> 00:27:38,700
Yeah.

411
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:40,700
Will he really be okay like that?

412
00:27:41,100 --> 00:27:44,520
He wants to die in the village of the
legendary Otori that he loves so much.

413
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:46,900
-Isn't that what he wants?
-Sis!

414
00:27:47,300 --> 00:27:48,880
I'm just joking.

415
00:27:50,200 --> 00:27:51,600
Yoichi.

416
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:56,920
Just where did you go?

417
00:27:57,740 --> 00:27:59,160
Where?

418
00:27:59,400 --> 00:28:01,720
I went to get my cigarettes
from a room.

419
00:28:01,880 --> 00:28:03,200
This.

420
00:28:06,820 --> 00:28:12,460
<i>We place a murder curse
upon the Wakura family...</i>

421
00:28:12,620 --> 00:28:14,180
<i>...who defiles our sacred land.</i>
"Curse"

422
00:28:14,560 --> 00:28:16,000
"Murder"

423
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:29,440
<i>The criminal most likely left this
fragment at the crime scene on purpose...</i>

424
00:28:29,440 --> 00:28:33,700
<i>...in order to scare Wakura
when he saw this word, "curse".</i>

425
00:28:34,380 --> 00:28:38,420
<i>And clearly, a portion of an entire passage.</i>

426
00:28:39,360 --> 00:28:42,120
<i>If my deduction is correct... </i>

427
00:28:42,280 --> 00:28:45,180
<i>...when the fragments are put back together,...</i>

428
00:28:45,180 --> 00:28:47,900
<i>...the criminal's true
motives will appear.</i>

429
00:29:03,900 --> 00:29:05,200
Hey!
"God's Perch Ruins"

430
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:07,500
Where are you?

431
00:29:09,120 --> 00:29:11,860
Calling me out in the middle
of the night like this.

432
00:29:13,060 --> 00:29:15,440
Is this about the
distribution of the property?

433
00:29:48,760 --> 00:29:50,180
That sound?

434
00:29:50,700 --> 00:29:53,700
The paper used for letter,
has no characteristics about it.

435
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:56,100
It's mostly made of old newspapers.

436
00:29:57,080 --> 00:30:01,020
We will never find the person who
issued this threatening letter like this.

437
00:30:02,420 --> 00:30:05,140
We have no choice, but to send it
to forensics and let them investigate it.

438
00:30:06,720 --> 00:30:07,800
Hey!

439
00:30:08,120 --> 00:30:10,800
The detective boy standing there,
were you listening?

440
00:30:11,340 --> 00:30:12,860
Ah...

441
00:30:15,340 --> 00:30:17,860
The Wakura chain has
4,000 branches across the country.

442
00:30:18,340 --> 00:30:20,020
10,000 employees.

443
00:30:20,560 --> 00:30:25,200
Well, given only just those, some
incident is bound to occur every day.

444
00:30:26,240 --> 00:30:32,680
If I could solve this case here
and that became well-known...

445
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:35,640
...I could be employed by them
as a special-adviser detective.

446
00:30:36,660 --> 00:30:39,900
The Special Adviser Detective,
Mori Kogoro is born!

447
00:30:40,380 --> 00:30:43,800
I'll collect consultant fees
one after the other!

448
00:30:50,220 --> 00:30:51,300
Eh?

449
00:30:51,740 --> 00:30:53,300
Is he serious?

450
00:30:54,100 --> 00:30:55,840
That’s fast...

451
00:31:01,060 --> 00:31:03,900
Somehow, I couldn't sleep.

452
00:31:05,240 --> 00:31:06,960
Ah.

453
00:31:30,900 --> 00:31:35,500
Because something like that happened...
will the festival be cancelled?

454
00:31:36,280 --> 00:31:37,660
Maybe.

455
00:31:38,060 --> 00:31:41,860
But, it only comes once every 300 years.

456
00:31:42,340 --> 00:31:44,760
Once every 300 years, huh?

457
00:31:45,700 --> 00:31:48,720
Shinichi, do you think a full solar
eclipse will really happen?

458
00:31:49,380 --> 00:31:51,700
A full eclipse would be impossible.

459
00:31:52,080 --> 00:31:55,000
Still, I am a little interested in
what might happen.

460
00:31:55,720 --> 00:31:59,920
Hmm...Is being a little
interested all there is?

461
00:32:02,380 --> 00:32:03,680
Eh?

462
00:32:05,180 --> 00:32:10,760
Look, um, well...there's that
romantic story to it, right?

463
00:32:14,860 --> 00:32:16,040
What was that?

464
00:32:19,120 --> 00:32:20,660
Nothing!

465
00:32:21,020 --> 00:32:23,840
What is it?
What are you so angry about?

466
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:33,500
<i>The lovers who exchange kisses
beneath the God's Perch...</i>

467
00:32:33,700 --> 00:32:37,560
<i>...will never be parted
and be married for life.</i>

468
00:32:39,320 --> 00:32:40,920
<i>Kiss...</i>

469
00:33:11,480 --> 00:33:12,980
Ryoji!

470
00:33:14,240 --> 00:33:17,660
Anyhow, we need to let
Captain Megure know.

471
00:33:18,140 --> 00:33:20,060
It's no good. Like I thought,
cell phones aren’t connected here.

472
00:33:20,220 --> 00:33:22,860
-I’ll go inform him.
-Please do.

473
00:33:36,980 --> 00:33:38,960
<i>Another one.</i>

474
00:33:39,240 --> 00:33:44,100
<i>Like I thought the criminal is leaving
one of these at each murder scene.</i>

475
00:33:49,340 --> 00:33:51,800
<i>Judging from the situation...</i>

476
00:33:51,920 --> 00:33:54,380
<i>...he couldn't have been killed
by being impaled.</i>

477
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:59,940
<i>So how did the criminal
get Ryoji up there?...</i>

478
00:34:00,760 --> 00:34:04,880
<i>And what is that sound...?</i>

479
00:34:12,680 --> 00:34:14,560
Shinichi.

480
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:18,700
The phones aren't working.

481
00:34:18,940 --> 00:34:21,080
Dad and the others are
investigating the cause right now.

482
00:34:21,420 --> 00:34:23,020
What was that?

483
00:34:26,160 --> 00:34:29,380
-Don't tell me...
-Wait, Shinichi!

484
00:34:39,140 --> 00:34:40,100
Ran!

485
00:34:40,300 --> 00:34:42,220
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

486
00:34:51,420 --> 00:34:54,260
-No way.
-We were too late.

487
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:56,660
Shinichi?

488
00:34:56,920 --> 00:35:01,100
The bridge didn't fall on its own.
The criminal cut it down.

489
00:35:02,160 --> 00:35:03,880
How did you know this would happen?

490
00:35:04,220 --> 00:35:06,400
When you told me
the phones weren't working...

491
00:35:06,600 --> 00:35:10,920
...I realized that the criminal was
trying to trap us here to this village.

492
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:15,680
Until all of his serial killings are over.

493
00:35:16,880 --> 00:35:19,880
All?
You mean it will continue?

494
00:35:20,220 --> 00:35:21,460
Yeah.

495
00:35:23,460 --> 00:35:25,740
Until the pieces are assembled.

496
00:35:32,060 --> 00:35:36,180
-Brother Ryoji! Brother!
-What?

497
00:35:37,480 --> 00:35:39,900
Then we can't leave this village?

498
00:35:40,060 --> 00:35:40,860
No!

499
00:35:41,080 --> 00:35:43,440
The radios at the police station
are also broken...

500
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:45,680
...and the phones can't be used, either.

501
00:35:46,080 --> 00:35:47,980
The radios, too?

502
00:35:49,140 --> 00:35:53,620
This is Lord Otori's curse.

503
00:35:54,020 --> 00:35:57,220
Lord Otori has gotten angry!

504
00:35:57,480 --> 00:36:00,440
Now, hurry and leave this village!

505
00:36:00,640 --> 00:36:02,640
That's right! Get out right now!

506
00:36:02,800 --> 00:36:05,900
Don't make Lord Otori any angrier!

507
00:36:06,060 --> 00:36:08,100
-Get out!
-Please calm down a little.

508
00:36:08,240 --> 00:36:11,840
Because we'll figure out how
to repair the bridge and phones.

509
00:36:11,980 --> 00:36:13,740
Please return to your homes for now.

510
00:36:13,900 --> 00:36:17,020
For now, please stay
in groups just in case...

511
00:36:17,160 --> 00:36:20,280
...and don't venture out alone.
Please.

512
00:36:21,760 --> 00:36:25,520
The suspension bridge to the other side
from the village has collapsed?

513
00:36:25,740 --> 00:36:26,860
Yeah.

514
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:31,980
That means the criminal let the
suspension bridge from the village fall.

515
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:34,240
-In other words...
-Yes.

516
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:37,960
The criminal is still in the village.

517
00:36:39,420 --> 00:36:41,020
Who will be next?

518
00:36:41,780 --> 00:36:43,600
Who will it be?

519
00:36:44,360 --> 00:36:48,780
It's just like the threatening letter.
Most likely the next one will be...

520
00:36:48,980 --> 00:36:52,220
Me or brother Yoichi...

521
00:36:53,500 --> 00:36:56,060
Or maybe you, Misa.

522
00:37:00,100 --> 00:37:02,180
We finished dinner at 9 pm.

523
00:37:02,460 --> 00:37:05,820
At that time, Ryoji was still here in the villa.

524
00:37:06,220 --> 00:37:07,820
Everyone saw that.

525
00:37:08,640 --> 00:37:12,800
Ran and I went out for a walk
and found his corpse at 11 pm.

526
00:37:13,900 --> 00:37:18,980
Let's confirm everyone’s alibis for those
2 hours, between 9 - 11 pm.

527
00:37:19,960 --> 00:37:21,360
Alibis, you say...

528
00:37:21,520 --> 00:37:23,740
Do you mean that one of us killed Ryoji?

529
00:37:23,840 --> 00:37:25,100
Yoichi.

530
00:37:25,280 --> 00:37:26,980
If you told us, would that cause
some trouble for you?

531
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:28,340
Ridiculous!

532
00:37:28,480 --> 00:37:32,900
Until around 10 pm, I was with
Ran and her mother talking.

533
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:35,000
But after that I went to sleep.

534
00:37:35,820 --> 00:37:37,820
I don't have an alibi.

535
00:37:38,460 --> 00:37:40,480
I was just in my room.

536
00:37:40,780 --> 00:37:43,500
It was the same for brother Yoichi
and Misa, wasn't it?

537
00:37:44,240 --> 00:37:48,100
But there's our father, too.

538
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:50,800
He has no alibi.

539
00:38:09,960 --> 00:38:11,560
This is...

540
00:38:16,200 --> 00:38:18,620
Shinichi, do you understand
what this means?

541
00:38:19,260 --> 00:38:23,260
If I'm not mistaken, this is "betrayal."

542
00:38:26,340 --> 00:38:28,020
This is "curse."

543
00:38:30,660 --> 00:38:33,140
Is this a man.

544
00:38:33,760 --> 00:38:35,880
Is he running?

545
00:38:36,540 --> 00:38:40,460
What sort of meaning
is there to this picture?

546
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:04,180
Ah, delicious!

547
00:39:04,780 --> 00:39:07,320
Misa, this was freshly-squeezed,
wasn't it?

548
00:39:07,780 --> 00:39:09,920
I'm a man who can tell the difference.

549
00:39:10,260 --> 00:39:12,320
It's just from a regular carton of milk.

550
00:39:13,600 --> 00:39:15,420
Geez... (mou...)

551
00:39:15,820 --> 00:39:18,900
"Moo"? Was that a pun?
That was a pun, right?

552
00:39:27,600 --> 00:39:29,120
Everyone.

553
00:39:29,500 --> 00:39:32,000
You don't seem to have
much of an appetite.

554
00:39:32,780 --> 00:39:36,900
Ryoji and Kosaka's murderer
hasn't been caught.

555
00:39:37,320 --> 00:39:40,860
The phones aren't working and
the suspension bridge has been felled.

556
00:39:41,400 --> 00:39:43,920
The radios at the
police station are broken.

557
00:39:44,520 --> 00:39:48,980
Well, if those were our only concerns,
this wouldn't be impossible.

558
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:52,540
But please everyone, don't worry.

559
00:39:53,640 --> 00:39:58,480
The name that resound around
the world, Mori Kogoro, is on your side.

560
00:40:01,920 --> 00:40:05,240
Just where in the world
does it resound?

561
00:40:05,820 --> 00:40:08,740
Does your world have
a radius of 1 meter?

562
00:40:09,020 --> 00:40:13,500
-Stop complaining about everything!
-Ah! It's only 50 cm! I’m sorry...

563
00:40:13,660 --> 00:40:15,560
There's something
I'd like to ask all of you.

564
00:40:15,800 --> 00:40:18,540
Was there anyone who bore
a grudge against Ryoji?

565
00:40:19,240 --> 00:40:20,660
No clue...

566
00:40:20,920 --> 00:40:22,500
He did a lot of things, but...

567
00:40:22,660 --> 00:40:25,680
...I don't think he made any enemies
who'd want to kill him.

568
00:40:25,960 --> 00:40:27,700
But, he was in debt, wasn't he?

569
00:40:28,540 --> 00:40:30,660
-In debt?
-Yes.

570
00:40:30,940 --> 00:40:35,380
Ryoji was managing a restaurant
separate from the Wakura chain...

571
00:40:35,580 --> 00:40:37,580
...but it didn't go well.

572
00:40:37,960 --> 00:40:41,060
I don't know the amount
of his debts, though.

573
00:40:41,540 --> 00:40:42,900
Is that so?

574
00:40:43,220 --> 00:40:46,760
By the way, what sort of work
do you do, Yoichi?

575
00:40:47,420 --> 00:40:51,820
Right now I'm raising funds to start
a business making earnings from stocks.

576
00:40:52,820 --> 00:40:54,960
Raising funds?

577
00:40:55,720 --> 00:40:59,960
Yoichi only wanted pocket money, so
he could make tiny trades over the Internet.

578
00:41:00,260 --> 00:41:03,480
Moreover, just the other day
you secretly went to Dad...

579
00:41:03,620 --> 00:41:06,180
...crying about how you have
suffered a huge loss in FX.

580
00:41:06,340 --> 00:41:08,800
That's better than some dull guy
who has to be financially supported.

581
00:41:09,320 --> 00:41:11,560
I heard your boyfriend's a musician
who hasn't even sold a song.

582
00:41:11,680 --> 00:41:14,340
-What did you say?!
-Stop it, both of you.

583
00:41:15,560 --> 00:41:19,700
Man. Why are you
interrogating one another?!

584
00:41:20,120 --> 00:41:22,040
You've still got a long way to go,
detective boy.

585
00:41:22,140 --> 00:41:24,900
Green. Too young.

586
00:41:28,560 --> 00:41:31,840
I already know who the criminal is.

587
00:41:33,040 --> 00:41:35,060
Who is the criminal?

588
00:41:36,040 --> 00:41:39,760
-The criminal is...
-The criminal is?

589
00:41:41,820 --> 00:41:45,240
The criminal is...

590
00:41:45,580 --> 00:41:50,600
-You, Yoichi.
-Huh? Me?

591
00:41:52,480 --> 00:41:54,980
This rare cigarette is yours, isn't it?

592
00:41:55,640 --> 00:41:59,320
I clearly saw you
smoking one yesterday.

593
00:41:59,780 --> 00:42:04,820
And I discovered this one at the site
where Ryoji was murdered.

594
00:42:05,680 --> 00:42:10,560
This great detective's eagle eye
doesn't miss anything!

595
00:42:10,720 --> 00:42:11,680
Give me a break!

596
00:42:12,240 --> 00:42:14,240
Just because I smoke
doesn't make me the murderer!

597
00:42:14,240 --> 00:42:16,660
Jerk! Do you intend
on denying it! You...

598
00:42:16,880 --> 00:42:19,300
I wonder if it is.

599
00:42:19,680 --> 00:42:24,940
Aren’t you going overboard,
accusing Yoichi of being at the scene...

600
00:42:25,160 --> 00:42:26,940
...just because of a cigarette butt?

601
00:42:27,180 --> 00:42:28,720
Huh?

602
00:42:29,580 --> 00:42:34,980
These butts were carelessly left
in every ashtray in the house.

603
00:42:35,220 --> 00:42:39,980
That means anyone who came into the
house would have been able to take one.

604
00:42:40,200 --> 00:42:42,780
-This doesn't mean anything.
-Ah! Hey, hey!

605
00:42:43,120 --> 00:42:47,200
You idiot!
My important evidence!

606
00:42:49,200 --> 00:42:51,540
I regret listening to him.

607
00:42:51,860 --> 00:42:56,840
Well, but Kosaka and Ryoji's death
would really make Yoichi happy though.

608
00:42:56,980 --> 00:42:57,820
What are you saying?

609
00:42:58,000 --> 00:43:01,380
-That'd be you Kotomi, wouldn't it?!
-Please, stop it you two.

610
00:43:10,920 --> 00:43:15,100
Um... Excuse me as well.
I'll go check on father.

611
00:43:20,200 --> 00:43:24,000
I have a favor to ask.
Could you keep an eye on Kotomi?

612
00:43:24,520 --> 00:43:25,680
All right.

613
00:43:25,900 --> 00:43:27,980
And Sonoko, Yoichi.

614
00:43:30,460 --> 00:43:36,080
-What about you, Shinichi?
-For me...Misa.

615
00:44:16,720 --> 00:44:19,540
-How is he?
-He seems to be sleeping well.

616
00:44:20,420 --> 00:44:21,880
I see.

617
00:44:24,700 --> 00:44:26,740
When the suspension bridge
will be restored?

618
00:44:27,040 --> 00:44:29,560
I want to take him to the hospital
as soon as possible.

619
00:44:33,740 --> 00:44:38,160
Kudo, please.
Hurry and catch the criminal.

620
00:44:40,140 --> 00:44:41,360
Yes.

621
00:44:45,340 --> 00:44:48,620
Misa...May I ask you a question?

622
00:44:49,260 --> 00:44:51,360
Kotomi mentioned this earlier.

623
00:44:52,460 --> 00:44:56,120
That if Kosaka and Ryoji were dead,
Yoichi would be happy.

624
00:44:56,280 --> 00:44:58,360
What did she mean by that?

625
00:45:03,760 --> 00:45:05,520
Misa.

626
00:45:10,840 --> 00:45:12,620
When my father declared...

627
00:45:12,760 --> 00:45:17,620
...he would invest his entire fortune
into investigating the Otori legend.

628
00:45:17,840 --> 00:45:19,940
My older brothers and sister
were opposed to it.

629
00:45:20,380 --> 00:45:23,720
At that time, my father told us...

630
00:45:24,000 --> 00:45:27,700
Kosaka should have been my son.

631
00:45:28,020 --> 00:45:31,020
I have no intention of leaving
any of you my assets.

632
00:45:31,680 --> 00:45:34,620
<i>I have no intention of leaving
any of you my assets.</i>

633
00:45:34,900 --> 00:45:37,760
Kosaka would use it more effectively.

634
00:45:38,480 --> 00:45:43,160
It seems that came as a great shock
to my brothers and sister.

635
00:45:43,640 --> 00:45:46,480
Brother Yoichi definitely
seems to be in debt.

636
00:45:46,820 --> 00:45:49,140
But, that's also why
it would be impossible for him...

637
00:45:49,280 --> 00:45:51,860
...to do anything to either
Kosaka or Brother Ryoji.

638
00:45:53,140 --> 00:45:57,300
Give me a break.
Won't you stop acting and wake up?

639
00:46:00,360 --> 00:46:03,800
I'm sure my sister wouldn't have
any reason to, either.

640
00:46:04,460 --> 00:46:08,820
However...after my father became
obsessed with the Otori legend...

641
00:46:09,040 --> 00:46:11,400
...our family’s relationship
had been strained.

642
00:46:11,740 --> 00:46:15,800
<i>"I will tell you how to claim
all of the inheritance."</i>

643
00:46:17,100 --> 00:46:23,400
<i>"Come to Jyugoya Falls'
God's Perch at 3 o'clock."</i>

644
00:46:26,940 --> 00:46:29,660
Thinking about
what might happen again...

645
00:46:29,900 --> 00:46:33,500
...worries and worries me.
How would it come to this?

646
00:46:36,660 --> 00:46:38,280
Thank you.

647
00:47:13,560 --> 00:47:18,440
The God's Perch is about 6 meters tall.

648
00:47:19,420 --> 00:47:26,060
Both Kosaka and Ryoji weighed
more than 60 kilos each, I think.

649
00:47:27,180 --> 00:47:31,980
How did the criminal impale them
up there at that height?

650
00:47:33,520 --> 00:47:35,520
You infidel!

651
00:47:37,060 --> 00:47:39,600
What are you doing?

652
00:47:40,360 --> 00:47:43,800
Do you want to be the fourth hayanie?

653
00:47:44,760 --> 00:47:46,460
Fourth?

654
00:47:46,760 --> 00:47:49,040
What do you mean by "the fourth"?

655
00:47:49,340 --> 00:47:53,880
Who other than Kosaka and Ryoji
were taken as hayanie?

656
00:47:54,460 --> 00:47:58,400
It's best not to wander around
the holy place without good reason.

657
00:47:58,640 --> 00:47:59,840
Please tell me!

658
00:48:00,020 --> 00:48:03,780
Who was it...and when did
he become a hayanie?!

659
00:48:04,000 --> 00:48:05,820
-Don't know.
-Please tell me!

660
00:48:06,020 --> 00:48:09,520
-I said I don't know, so I don't know!
-Please! Please tell me!

661
00:48:09,900 --> 00:48:12,920
The criminal is still...
He’s definitely still in this village!

662
00:48:15,480 --> 00:48:18,400
This isn't the work of a human.

663
00:48:19,360 --> 00:48:21,940
It's Lord Otori's curse.

664
00:48:23,320 --> 00:48:30,900
The Wakura clan set off Lord Otori's
wrath and made themselves hayanie.

665
00:48:34,940 --> 00:48:37,440
The festival will be soon.

666
00:48:39,160 --> 00:48:43,420
What's more, the full solar eclipse
that only happens once every 300 years.

667
00:48:43,660 --> 00:48:46,640
And Lord Otori will certainly appear!

668
00:48:48,480 --> 00:48:49,980
Shinichi!

669
00:48:50,780 --> 00:48:52,600
-What happened?
-Sorry.

670
00:48:52,780 --> 00:48:56,000
When I took my eyes off her,
Kotomi disappeared.

671
00:48:58,880 --> 00:49:00,060
Over there!

672
00:49:09,400 --> 00:49:10,980
Kotomi, are you okay?

673
00:49:19,620 --> 00:49:21,020
Ah, what...

674
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:23,880
I was just a little startled.

675
00:49:24,700 --> 00:49:26,840
Thank goodness nothing happened.

676
00:50:05,340 --> 00:50:08,060
Shinichi?! Kotomi!

677
00:50:08,640 --> 00:50:10,560
Shinichi!

678
00:50:24,300 --> 00:50:26,460
Kudo! Kudo!

679
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:33,920
-Ouch...
-Are you okay?

680
00:50:34,340 --> 00:50:36,560
-Somewhat.
-Thank goodness.

681
00:50:36,820 --> 00:50:40,600
-Kotomi, are you hurt?
-No. I'm really very sorry.

682
00:50:40,940 --> 00:50:44,040
It felt like I flew for a moment...

683
00:50:44,400 --> 00:50:45,700
Flew?

684
00:50:46,020 --> 00:50:48,940
What on earth is going on?
What, what is it?

685
00:50:49,380 --> 00:50:53,560
-Where's Ran?
-She was running off in that direction.

686
00:51:25,680 --> 00:51:27,100
Ran!

687
00:51:28,700 --> 00:51:30,200
Ran!

688
00:51:35,440 --> 00:51:39,280
Ran! Ah~!

689
00:51:43,960 --> 00:51:47,160
Ouch...

690
00:51:52,250 --> 00:51:53,260
Ran!

691
00:51:54,330 --> 00:51:55,770
Uncle?

692
00:51:56,350 --> 00:51:59,880
Ran! Are you okay, Ran!

693
00:52:02,010 --> 00:52:03,800
Are you okay?
Are you hurt?

694
00:52:03,960 --> 00:52:06,840
Shinichi...
I'm fine.

695
00:52:07,880 --> 00:52:10,200
Ah... geez.

696
00:52:12,080 --> 00:52:15,870
But, I kicked the criminal's
right hand right off.

697
00:52:16,280 --> 00:52:19,240
Ran...why did you do something
reckless on your own for?

698
00:52:20,140 --> 00:52:21,260
Sorry.

699
00:52:23,180 --> 00:52:26,120
Uncle? Uncles? Uncle?!

700
00:52:26,720 --> 00:52:29,210
Dad, what are you doing here?

701
00:52:29,640 --> 00:52:31,120
Dad!

702
00:52:36,560 --> 00:52:39,610
What is this? Making us worry.

703
00:52:39,770 --> 00:52:42,000
I really don't believe this.

704
00:52:56,190 --> 00:52:57,340
It's wet.

705
00:52:59,120 --> 00:53:00,160
No way.

706
00:53:01,640 --> 00:53:06,300
Oh no, I'm drenched! Why?
It's been sunny all day today.

707
00:53:16,430 --> 00:53:18,090
Don't catch a cold.

708
00:53:19,930 --> 00:53:21,360
Thank you.

709
00:53:22,090 --> 00:53:25,960
-But then you'll get cold, Shinichi.
-Fool, I'll be fine.

710
00:53:42,090 --> 00:53:44,600
Thank goodness I'm not alone.

711
00:53:45,800 --> 00:53:48,090
You’re here with me.

712
00:53:49,950 --> 00:53:53,390
Even so, it's pitiful that we are
stuck here and I can't rescue you.

713
00:53:53,600 --> 00:53:57,280
That's not true.
I'm happy that you came.

714
00:54:00,840 --> 00:54:05,870
But...even if it hadn't been me...

715
00:54:06,160 --> 00:54:09,360
You would have rescued
anyone, wouldn't you?

716
00:54:13,600 --> 00:54:16,090
I...

717
00:54:27,720 --> 00:54:30,750
-Did you see that just now? A tanuki.
-That must be a raccoon.

718
00:54:34,590 --> 00:54:35,800
Raccoon?

719
00:54:36,200 --> 00:54:39,390
-Dad, are you alright?
-You said raccoon just now.

720
00:54:39,530 --> 00:54:41,900
-Uncle?
-Where did it go?

721
00:54:42,030 --> 00:54:45,440
If I can catch that raccoon,
I can substitute it for Pascal.

722
00:54:45,630 --> 00:54:46,730
Are you sleep talking?

723
00:54:46,880 --> 00:54:50,040
What's this 'substitute Pascal' talk?
Raccoons are usually called Rascal.

724
00:54:50,140 --> 00:54:52,000
This one's Pascal!

725
00:54:52,570 --> 00:54:56,680
Anyhow, I was chasing after
this raccoon and I ended up down here...

726
00:54:56,810 --> 00:54:58,110
Get ahold of yourself, Dad!

727
00:54:58,320 --> 00:54:59,960
Pascal...

728
00:55:00,460 --> 00:55:04,650
-What about Pascal?
-The French philosopher and physicist.

729
00:55:05,180 --> 00:55:08,940
Pascal's law is the basis
for fluid dynamics...

730
00:55:09,150 --> 00:55:11,130
Mom!

731
00:55:11,420 --> 00:55:14,590
-Auntie!
-Are you okay?

732
00:55:14,840 --> 00:55:17,240
Hey! Hurry and do
something about this!

733
00:55:17,470 --> 00:55:20,700
Say, what are you doing
down there?

734
00:55:21,200 --> 00:55:23,150
Ran's an adult already...

735
00:55:23,260 --> 00:55:25,850
...so if you bother her
anymore, she'll hate you.

736
00:55:26,400 --> 00:55:30,120
That was a big chance
for you two be alone, right?

737
00:55:30,600 --> 00:55:31,710
It wasn't like that!

738
00:55:31,800 --> 00:55:35,930
Itchy, itchy, itchy!

739
00:55:36,860 --> 00:55:39,930
Pascal! Pascal, where are you?

740
00:55:40,750 --> 00:55:44,010
Pascal!!

741
00:55:45,840 --> 00:55:48,120
Why did you go to
that place all by yourself for?

742
00:55:49,200 --> 00:55:51,980
-I was called.
-You were called?

743
00:55:52,280 --> 00:55:53,850
-By who?
-I don't know.

744
00:55:54,200 --> 00:55:56,520
Next thing I know
it's already in my pocket.

745
00:55:56,920 --> 00:56:00,780
-Do you still have that letter?
-I threw it away!

746
00:56:02,510 --> 00:56:04,190
What was written in the letter?

747
00:56:06,600 --> 00:56:07,850
Sister?

748
00:56:09,260 --> 00:56:13,840
"I will tell you how to claim
all of the inheritance."

749
00:56:15,630 --> 00:56:17,040
What's that?

750
00:56:17,370 --> 00:56:19,840
Was the one targeting the inheritance
not me, but you, Kotomi?

751
00:56:19,900 --> 00:56:22,110
You're wrong!
I wouldn't consider such a thing.

752
00:56:23,260 --> 00:56:28,750
However...whoever called me away
may be the one who killed Ryoji.

753
00:56:29,900 --> 00:56:33,920
-The clue to the criminal...
-What's this 'clue'?

754
00:56:34,170 --> 00:56:35,710
Your target is the inheritance!

755
00:56:36,010 --> 00:56:37,530
Please wait, you two.

756
00:56:37,710 --> 00:56:41,260
Inheritance, inheritance!
Dad's not even dead yet!

757
00:56:54,970 --> 00:56:58,920
I'm sorry...that you had
to see something unsightly.

758
00:57:17,950 --> 00:57:19,160
Man?

759
00:57:22,840 --> 00:57:23,980
Bird.

760
00:57:28,800 --> 00:57:29,930
Curse.

761
00:57:34,810 --> 00:57:35,950
Betrayal.

762
00:57:37,400 --> 00:57:39,770
It just needs one more
piece to complete it.

763
00:57:40,240 --> 00:57:46,090
In other words...one more
incident will definitely occur.

764
00:57:51,580 --> 00:57:53,420
I will definitely stop it.

765
00:57:59,200 --> 00:58:02,750
<i>Do you want to be the fourth hayanie?</i>

766
00:58:03,770 --> 00:58:08,300
<i>Who other than Kosaka and Ryoji
were taken as hayanie?</i>

767
00:58:28,160 --> 00:58:31,050
Ah...Good morning.

768
00:58:32,000 --> 00:58:33,500
Good morning.

769
00:58:34,280 --> 00:58:35,770
Come in.

770
00:58:36,670 --> 00:58:37,920
Did something happen?

771
00:58:38,250 --> 00:58:41,050
There's something I'd like you to tell me.

772
00:58:41,440 --> 00:58:42,490
Huh?

773
00:58:42,780 --> 00:58:44,700
At the God's Perch before all this...

774
00:58:44,830 --> 00:58:46,700
...there was someone else who
was a hayanie, wasn't there?

775
00:58:52,040 --> 00:58:53,400
There was?

776
00:58:53,870 --> 00:58:55,260
Leave!

777
00:58:56,840 --> 00:58:59,960
-Please answer me.
-You’re noisy!

778
00:59:00,640 --> 00:59:04,940
It's when Tokyo people like you
come that bad things happen!

779
00:59:06,040 --> 00:59:07,320
Tokyo people?

780
00:59:07,720 --> 00:59:10,300
By "Tokyo people,"
do you mean Mr.Wakura?

781
00:59:10,600 --> 00:59:14,000
Could it be that Mr.Wakura
had been to this village previously?

782
00:59:14,090 --> 00:59:16,400
I have nothing to tell you.

783
00:59:16,560 --> 00:59:17,920
Takezo.

784
00:59:18,570 --> 00:59:19,930
Listen!

785
00:59:20,190 --> 00:59:23,180
Once that suspension bridge's
repaired, hurry and get out of here!

786
00:59:25,530 --> 00:59:28,010
I'm sorry. I was just a little
interested in something.

787
00:59:28,320 --> 00:59:30,560
The references on the history
of the village are all here.

788
00:59:30,810 --> 00:59:33,660
-Would they be helpful?
-Thank you.

789
00:59:58,030 --> 00:59:59,920
"Jyugoya Village Town Hall"

790
01:00:07,260 --> 01:00:08,960
For records on the deceased...

791
01:00:09,080 --> 01:00:11,740
...I guess that I still have to go
to the Administrative Hall.

792
01:00:12,600 --> 01:00:13,800
Oh?

793
01:00:14,430 --> 01:00:15,870
Misa?

794
01:00:30,320 --> 01:00:33,840
This is...a bronze mirror?

795
01:01:00,890 --> 01:01:02,520
<i>I see.</i>

796
01:01:02,830 --> 01:01:08,400
<i>These were opposing mirrors
connected from back to back.</i>

797
01:01:19,200 --> 01:01:20,810
"[Surname] found at the Fobina ruins"

798
01:01:23,980 --> 01:01:25,160
Man?

799
01:01:28,190 --> 01:01:30,560
<i>Similarities between the
Mayan Civilization's Fobina Ruins...</i>

800
01:01:30,700 --> 01:01:33,360
<i>...and Jyugoya Village Ruins.</i>

801
01:01:36,030 --> 01:01:40,430
<i>Mayan Civilization's Fobina Ruins.</i>

802
01:01:40,730 --> 01:01:43,920
<i>Jyugoya Village’s Monster Bird.</i>

803
01:01:44,810 --> 01:01:49,310
<i>Light of the Sun reaches the pyramid.</i>

804
01:01:49,480 --> 01:01:54,300
<i>The bronze mirror
resonates on God's Perch.</i>

805
01:01:55,040 --> 01:01:57,020
<i>Coming down from Heaven.</i>

806
01:01:58,360 --> 01:02:00,600
<i>Flying down from Heaven.</i>

807
01:02:01,530 --> 01:02:04,730
<i>Sacrifice to God.</i>

808
01:02:05,530 --> 01:02:07,920
<i>Hayanie.</i>

809
01:02:22,350 --> 01:02:24,010
"Fobina Ruins"

810
01:02:29,880 --> 01:02:31,880
Underground sewers?

811
01:02:38,560 --> 01:02:41,840
<i>The God's Perches are landmarks
for underground sewers?!</i>

812
01:02:48,300 --> 01:02:51,440
<i>First...This is where Kosaka died.</i>

813
01:02:54,000 --> 01:02:56,380
<i>And here is Ryoji's.</i>

814
01:02:58,480 --> 01:03:01,020
<i>And here is where Kotomi flew...</i>

815
01:03:47,680 --> 01:03:50,400
<i>Konno Machiko</i>.
"Konno Machiko 1986 deceased"

816
01:03:55,820 --> 01:03:57,560
Ha! Don't come near!

817
01:03:57,720 --> 01:04:01,320
This is a place
where the Wakuras and...

818
01:04:01,420 --> 01:04:03,240
...those associated with them
cannot come near!

819
01:04:03,680 --> 01:04:04,970
Leave!

820
01:04:05,420 --> 01:04:10,320
Are you saying that this person’s death
is somehow related to Mr. Wakura?

821
01:04:13,550 --> 01:04:15,280
Is that so?

822
01:04:16,430 --> 01:04:20,440
Was this person a hayanie before?

823
01:04:22,430 --> 01:04:23,900
Please answer me!

824
01:04:29,500 --> 01:04:36,080
Just how much do you know
about the legend of this village?

825
01:04:37,660 --> 01:04:42,750
That long ago, it's said a giant
Mozu bird made a hayanie out of a person.

826
01:04:44,220 --> 01:04:48,540
The bronze mirror in the shrine
resonates with the God's Perch...

827
01:04:48,670 --> 01:04:52,570
...once every 300 years
to cause a full solar eclipse.

828
01:04:52,940 --> 01:04:58,430
And that lovers who exchange
kisses under the Perch...

829
01:04:58,560 --> 01:05:01,550
...will never leave
one another their entire lives.

830
01:05:04,430 --> 01:05:05,640
I see.

831
01:05:06,380 --> 01:05:08,190
Is that everything about the legend?

832
01:05:08,590 --> 01:05:10,350
Isn't there still something left hidden?

833
01:05:10,590 --> 01:05:12,460
That's everything.

834
01:05:15,160 --> 01:05:17,720
If you know the legend...

835
01:05:17,840 --> 01:05:20,880
...then don't let yourself
be attacked by Lord Otori.

836
01:05:23,080 --> 01:05:25,130
Be quiet.

837
01:05:26,750 --> 01:05:28,510
A person can't die from a legend.

838
01:05:29,550 --> 01:05:32,350
-Please tell me everything you know.
-Annoying!

839
01:05:32,920 --> 01:05:36,200
Just before a murder occurs, the sound
of something creaking is heard.

840
01:05:36,330 --> 01:05:37,660
Just what is that?

841
01:05:38,560 --> 01:05:43,900
It's Lord Otori's angry voice.

842
01:05:59,400 --> 01:06:01,150
You've realized it, haven't you?

843
01:06:06,560 --> 01:06:10,270
-Are you okay?
-Yeah, I'm all better now.

844
01:06:14,110 --> 01:06:17,370
Wakura, you mentioned that you have
been investigating the Otori legend...

845
01:06:17,450 --> 01:06:21,040
...and legends of monster birds
since your schooldays, correct?

846
01:06:23,280 --> 01:06:24,990
And?

847
01:06:26,200 --> 01:06:30,840
Have you been to
Jyugoya Village previously?

848
01:06:32,920 --> 01:06:34,320
What are you getting at?

849
01:06:37,080 --> 01:06:41,040
That bronze mirror...

850
01:06:41,450 --> 01:06:45,050
Could it be that this is the original
bronze mirror from Mozutobi Shrine?

851
01:06:51,770 --> 01:06:53,690
Konno Machiko.

852
01:06:58,040 --> 01:07:00,030
You knew her, didn't you?

853
01:07:02,720 --> 01:07:08,350
You know who
the criminal is, don't you?

854
01:08:52,560 --> 01:08:54,110
<i>Is that so?</i>

855
01:08:57,550 --> 01:08:59,820
As I thought...

856
01:09:02,540 --> 01:09:04,240
<i>I know the trick now.</i>

857
01:09:05,450 --> 01:09:08,190
<i>Like I thought, the criminal...</i>

858
01:09:08,320 --> 01:09:10,010
<i>There's no mistake
that it was that person.</i>

859
01:09:10,240 --> 01:09:11,710
The people of the village are worried that...

860
01:09:11,800 --> 01:09:15,100
...it will be dangerous if 
you attend the festival.

861
01:09:15,240 --> 01:09:16,510
That's right!
It's best that you not to come.

862
01:09:16,600 --> 01:09:18,650
Is there a law that
forbids me from coming?

863
01:09:18,990 --> 01:09:20,040
Huh?!

864
01:09:20,560 --> 01:09:22,840
You outsider, acting all great!

865
01:09:24,010 --> 01:09:25,260
Outsider?

866
01:09:26,860 --> 01:09:29,210
I am currently the largest landowner
in this village, you know?

867
01:09:30,400 --> 01:09:32,760
You will become
Lord Otori’s his hayanie...

868
01:09:32,880 --> 01:09:35,180
Whatever anyone else may say,
I will attend the festival.

869
01:09:35,440 --> 01:09:38,220
I understand.
I will protect you on that day.

870
01:09:43,020 --> 01:09:44,590
I will be under your care.

871
01:09:46,400 --> 01:09:49,660
-All of you, go home for today.
-Wait a minute!

872
01:09:49,790 --> 01:09:51,960
You’re causing trouble.
Go home. Let’s go.

873
01:09:57,320 --> 01:10:00,510
This murder case hasn't ended yet.

874
01:10:03,200 --> 01:10:07,920
Because the criminal's primary
goal hasn't been achieved yet.

875
01:10:09,370 --> 01:10:12,160
What is the criminal's goal?

876
01:10:29,680 --> 01:10:31,980
"The Day of the Festival"

877
01:10:45,100 --> 01:10:48,780
Somehow, this performance is strange.

878
01:10:49,930 --> 01:10:51,050
Yeah.

879
01:10:52,490 --> 01:10:54,490
Will we be okay!?

880
01:10:55,080 --> 01:10:58,400
Don't worry.
I’m sure that it’ll go well.

881
01:11:19,960 --> 01:11:23,820
"Inner Sanctuary God's Perch"

882
01:11:32,160 --> 01:11:38,240
The village chief and his companions...

883
01:11:38,460 --> 01:11:40,970
Come forward!

884
01:11:46,350 --> 01:11:48,860
Right now, I am
the owner of this village.

885
01:12:37,630 --> 01:12:44,120
Calm down. Calm down.
Lord Otori, calm down...

886
01:12:44,620 --> 01:12:50,460
Calm down, calm down.
Calm down, Lord Otori.

887
01:14:08,110 --> 01:14:09,440
No!

888
01:14:10,970 --> 01:14:12,890
Wa... Wakura!

889
01:14:13,230 --> 01:14:14,510
Wakura!

890
01:14:23,660 --> 01:14:25,400
Huh? It's not!

891
01:14:33,180 --> 01:14:34,560
Dad!

892
01:14:37,690 --> 01:14:38,960
Indeed...

893
01:14:39,080 --> 01:14:41,880
With impossible crime
like being cursed by Lord Otori...

894
01:14:42,300 --> 01:14:46,090
You can't help but think this couldn't
possibly be the act of a human.

895
01:14:47,870 --> 01:14:49,400
However...

896
01:14:49,530 --> 01:14:55,790
The criminal made use of a certain
power to make Kosaka and Ryoji...

897
01:14:55,930 --> 01:15:01,660
...fly up onto the God's Perch where
they were then impaled and killed.

898
01:15:03,850 --> 01:15:05,360
Just like that.

899
01:15:05,760 --> 01:15:12,540
When pressure is applied to water
or air in an airtight container...

900
01:15:12,760 --> 01:15:16,830
That pressure is transmitted to every
part of the fluid with the same energy.

901
01:15:17,020 --> 01:15:19,560
It is a trick utilizing Pascal's principle.

902
01:15:20,060 --> 01:15:23,520
There is a network of underground
sewers beneath this village.

903
01:15:24,190 --> 01:15:27,850
The criminal used that to commit murder.

904
01:15:28,280 --> 01:15:34,000
First, water from the river is channeled
into a hole and temporarily held there.

905
01:15:34,880 --> 01:15:37,200
When the hole’s trapdoor
is opened remotely...

906
01:15:37,310 --> 01:15:39,290
...the water flows down
the hole all at once.

907
01:15:39,640 --> 01:15:41,820
This creates a huge amount
of air pressure.

908
01:15:42,890 --> 01:15:46,040
This air pressure then
spreads through the sewer...

909
01:15:46,160 --> 01:15:48,060
...springing up this slate.

910
01:15:49,470 --> 01:15:52,060
That creaking sound you hear is...

911
01:15:52,140 --> 01:15:54,730
...the sound of the hole’s
trapdoor being opened.

912
01:16:01,450 --> 01:16:04,680
The first victim was Kosaka.

913
01:16:05,980 --> 01:16:10,520
But at that time, the criminal
was actually targeting Misa.

914
01:16:13,180 --> 01:16:16,780
The criminal, his target being Misa...

915
01:16:16,880 --> 01:16:19,580
...chose the timing when
she was standing on this slate...

916
01:16:19,690 --> 01:16:21,630
...and pushed the remote control.

917
01:16:23,100 --> 01:16:28,780
However, his timing was slightly off
and Kosaka who became the victim.

918
01:16:29,950 --> 01:16:33,930
With that failure, the criminal decided
to summon just his target alone.

919
01:16:34,700 --> 01:16:36,520
"Hey, where are you?"

920
01:16:42,560 --> 01:16:44,140
Ryoji...

921
01:16:46,360 --> 01:16:50,440
In the same way,
his next target, Kotomi but...

922
01:16:50,590 --> 01:16:52,570
...that attempt ended in failure.

923
01:16:55,720 --> 01:16:59,470
That was because there wasn't
enough air pressure.

924
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:03,980
The previous night, Ran had stumbled
over the slate, causing it to slip.

925
01:17:05,160 --> 01:17:08,880
And the criminal hadn't noticed that.

926
01:17:09,960 --> 01:17:13,560
Lastly, the criminal targeted Wakura.

927
01:17:15,820 --> 01:17:17,870
The moment that darkness fell...

928
01:17:17,980 --> 01:17:20,350
...the criminal pressed the remote switch.

929
01:17:26,720 --> 01:17:30,910
However, that darkness was...

930
01:17:31,000 --> 01:17:34,830
...a false solar eclipse created
by Ran and Sonoko.

931
01:17:35,980 --> 01:17:40,160
The criminal had unknowingly
fallen into my trap.

932
01:17:43,900 --> 01:17:47,040
The criminal...

933
01:17:47,130 --> 01:17:48,330
...is you.

934
01:17:54,400 --> 01:17:58,510
-Patrolman Haji.
-Why...?

935
01:17:59,230 --> 01:18:00,330
Why?

936
01:18:00,860 --> 01:18:03,080
Eh?
What evidence do you have?

937
01:18:06,880 --> 01:18:08,960
This is the evidence.

938
01:18:11,470 --> 01:18:15,950
-Ouch!
-Is your hand okay?

939
01:18:17,950 --> 01:18:20,140
Although you are a right-handed person...

940
01:18:20,250 --> 01:18:22,480
...you blocked with your right
hand when Ran kicked...

941
01:18:22,600 --> 01:18:24,270
...and held the screwdriver
with your left hand, right.

942
01:18:24,670 --> 01:18:27,420
<i>Ah, good morning.</i>

943
01:18:29,200 --> 01:18:33,740
What you were fixing
that time wasn't the radio.

944
01:18:34,860 --> 01:18:36,890
But the remote control.

945
01:18:46,700 --> 01:18:50,400
The reason you were attacking
the Wakura family was…

946
01:18:50,590 --> 01:18:52,160
Konno Machko.

947
01:18:54,040 --> 01:18:55,950
Her death is related to this, correct?

948
01:18:58,570 --> 01:19:03,560
30 years ago...
Machiko fell in love with Wakura...

949
01:19:03,770 --> 01:19:06,650
And was the woman
he promised eternal love to.

950
01:19:14,300 --> 01:19:17,240
He betrayed my mother
and abandoned her.

951
01:19:20,200 --> 01:19:23,630
Mom believed in his oath…

952
01:19:23,840 --> 01:19:27,610
Waited...waited and
kept on waiting for him.

953
01:19:29,000 --> 01:19:30,970
I thought so.

954
01:19:33,520 --> 01:19:35,040
Patrolman Haji...

955
01:19:35,210 --> 01:19:40,280
Machiko was your real mother, wasn't she?

956
01:19:41,920 --> 01:19:46,810
Around her memorial there were
flowers and Policeman Haji's footprints.

957
01:19:47,440 --> 01:19:51,630
At the time of Machiko's death,
Haji would have been 4 or 5 years old.

958
01:19:52,400 --> 01:19:55,130
Even today, you still come
visit her grave.

959
01:19:55,240 --> 01:19:57,930
Even after she died
when you were 4 to 5 years old.

960
01:19:58,090 --> 01:20:01,630
That would be unthinkable unless she
had been anyone but your real mother.

961
01:20:03,930 --> 01:20:07,960
You were really that
boy back then, weren't you?

962
01:20:16,880 --> 01:20:19,740
<i>25 years ago...</i>

963
01:20:20,040 --> 01:20:22,760
<i>Machiko suddenly appeared before me.</i>

964
01:20:22,970 --> 01:20:24,360
<i>Who is this child?</i>

965
01:20:24,990 --> 01:20:27,260
She was with a small child.

966
01:20:28,760 --> 01:20:30,590
A relative's child.

967
01:20:38,920 --> 01:20:42,960
This is the shrine’s heirloom bronze
mirror that you wanted to see.

968
01:20:43,160 --> 01:20:46,080
At the time, my business
was gaining momentum...

969
01:20:46,260 --> 01:20:49,240
...and had been the attention
of the mass media.

970
01:20:50,500 --> 01:20:55,960
I was under the impression Machiko
had come to extort money from me.

971
01:21:03,760 --> 01:21:07,120
Mom didn't turn the bronze mirror over
to you because she wanted your money!

972
01:21:08,000 --> 01:21:13,740
She just...
wanted you to remember...

973
01:21:13,920 --> 01:21:16,840
...the vow of love
you had made to her.

974
01:21:23,740 --> 01:21:25,720
My betrayed mother…

975
01:21:25,860 --> 01:21:28,500
...embracing the other half
of the bronze mirror.

976
01:21:58,960 --> 01:22:06,520
I am really...really sorry.

977
01:22:08,560 --> 01:22:10,280
How terrible.

978
01:22:13,040 --> 01:22:15,520
All of the criminal's crimes were...

979
01:22:15,700 --> 01:22:18,520
...to remind Wakura of
his betrayal of Machiko.

980
01:22:19,320 --> 01:22:21,360
And to take revenge for it.

981
01:22:28,740 --> 01:22:31,580
It was my mistake
has led to all of this.

982
01:22:33,240 --> 01:22:37,480
My mistakes has made me...

983
01:22:41,720 --> 01:22:46,500
Lost Ryoji... also lost Kosaka.

984
01:22:48,060 --> 01:22:54,200
And...I had left Machiko to die.

985
01:22:55,040 --> 01:22:57,520
Having been in love during
the days of your youth...

986
01:22:57,660 --> 01:23:02,080
...isn't reason for you
to blame yourself.

987
01:23:03,140 --> 01:23:08,380
But...it's just that
a woman’s life...

988
01:23:08,540 --> 01:23:10,680
...had been driven mad by it.

989
01:23:11,180 --> 01:23:15,360
Your lover's feelings were
too strong for her to bear.

990
01:23:19,280 --> 01:23:24,780
It...wasn't only
Machiko's life. but...

991
01:23:26,660 --> 01:23:30,140
Also your life which
I had messed up.

992
01:23:35,180 --> 01:23:38,640
Are you...

993
01:23:38,820 --> 01:23:42,140
Could it be that you are
mine and Machiko's...

994
01:23:44,580 --> 01:23:45,960
I have no father.

995
01:23:46,440 --> 01:23:48,760
I will never acknowledge
you as my father!

996
01:23:49,400 --> 01:23:51,040
Patrolman Haji!

997
01:23:51,620 --> 01:23:55,800
I spoke to Wakura
about my reasoning.

998
01:23:56,400 --> 01:23:58,800
Wakura says that...

999
01:23:58,960 --> 01:24:02,460
...he doesn’t want you
to commit any more crimes.

1000
01:24:02,860 --> 01:24:08,660
By that he risked himself
to cooperate with me.

1001
01:24:32,200 --> 01:24:35,840
What a sad, lonely picture.

1002
01:24:38,040 --> 01:24:39,680
Policeman Haji.

1003
01:24:39,960 --> 01:24:47,080
To you...this crying woman was
just like your mother, Machiko.

1004
01:24:49,760 --> 01:24:52,360
These two bronze mirrors...

1005
01:24:52,480 --> 01:24:55,960
...when back to back, express
the full details of the legend.

1006
01:24:57,440 --> 01:25:02,640
The bronze mirror Wakura had,
contains the character for "man"...

1007
01:25:02,840 --> 01:25:04,780
...as the one who
accomplished a betrayal.

1008
01:25:05,900 --> 01:25:11,660
On this bronze mirror, this character
perhaps stands for "woman."

1009
01:25:13,040 --> 01:25:15,340
This is the woman’s full account.

1010
01:25:15,860 --> 01:25:17,760
What do you mean?

1011
01:25:19,740 --> 01:25:26,720
Otori is the incarnation of the
woman who was betrayed by her lover.

1012
01:25:28,940 --> 01:25:31,560
That's been handed down
generation to generation.

1013
01:25:34,560 --> 01:25:36,460
Long ago...

1014
01:25:36,720 --> 01:25:42,780
The young couple had vowed and
kissed under the God's Perch.

1015
01:25:43,460 --> 01:25:46,300
But the man abandoned
the woman and ran away.

1016
01:25:47,520 --> 01:25:53,700
For the woman...
her passions turned into wings...

1017
01:25:53,900 --> 01:25:57,700
...and she became
the huge, ugly Otori...

1018
01:25:57,920 --> 01:26:01,080
...to attack the man
who had betrayed her.

1019
01:26:02,560 --> 01:26:11,460
The woman is said to have become
the Otori to curse and consume the man.

1020
01:26:11,800 --> 01:26:15,220
Was the reason you wouldn't
explain all the details of the legend…

1021
01:26:15,420 --> 01:26:17,920
...to protect Patrolman Haji?

1022
01:26:19,540 --> 01:26:23,000
I...

1023
01:26:23,220 --> 01:26:29,080
Took pity on this child and
raised him with my own hand.

1024
01:26:30,240 --> 01:26:32,340
So that's it.

1025
01:26:33,260 --> 01:26:37,300
So when you told the Wakura family
members to leave this village…

1026
01:26:37,440 --> 01:26:39,140
Was it because you didn't
want Patrolman Haji...

1027
01:26:39,300 --> 01:26:42,080
...repeating his crimes
any more, wasn't it?

1028
01:26:46,060 --> 01:26:48,000
Mom...

1029
01:26:50,380 --> 01:26:53,100
Mom, I'm sorry.

1030
01:27:27,560 --> 01:27:33,340
After 25 years, the true
bronze mirror has returned.

1031
01:28:35,040 --> 01:28:36,500
Ah...

1032
01:28:43,860 --> 01:28:45,900
A full solar eclipse.

1033
01:29:03,780 --> 01:29:05,460
It's Machiko!

1034
01:29:06,940 --> 01:29:11,340
Machiko has come back
as the birds!

1035
01:29:27,960 --> 01:29:30,680
A swarm of birds?

1036
01:29:33,880 --> 01:29:35,680
Birds...

1037
01:29:35,860 --> 01:29:38,300
Did a swarm of birds
block out the sun?

1038
01:29:39,480 --> 01:29:41,540
That's incredibly mysterious.

1039
01:29:48,460 --> 01:29:49,600
Captain Megure?

1040
01:29:49,900 --> 01:29:51,580
How long have you been here?

1041
01:29:52,000 --> 01:29:54,640
We finally repaired
the suspension bridge.

1042
01:29:56,100 --> 01:29:59,000
I heard the entire story.

1043
01:30:02,660 --> 01:30:04,460
Good work, good work.

1044
01:30:09,660 --> 01:30:13,080
Seriously?
He was here...

1045
01:30:23,360 --> 01:30:25,420
That was a sad case, wasn't it?

1046
01:30:28,320 --> 01:30:29,260
Yeah.

1047
01:30:33,740 --> 01:30:36,520
-Say, Ran.
-Huh?

1048
01:30:37,960 --> 01:30:40,440
About what you said that time.

1049
01:30:42,200 --> 01:30:43,880
That time?

1050
01:30:44,340 --> 01:30:45,920
When we had fallen into that hole.

1051
01:30:46,160 --> 01:30:47,980
<i>I'm happy that you came.</i>

1052
01:30:51,200 --> 01:30:56,460
<i>But...even if it hadn't been me...</i>

1053
01:30:56,660 --> 01:31:00,120
<i>You would have rescued
anyone, wouldn't you?</i>

1054
01:31:01,480 --> 01:31:03,980
I...

1055
01:31:06,320 --> 01:31:07,480
Yeah.

1056
01:31:10,360 --> 01:31:12,280
...did it because it was you, Ran.

1057
01:31:29,160 --> 01:31:31,040
I told you, it's Pascal!

1058
01:31:31,160 --> 01:31:33,800
A raccoon is called Rascal!

1059
01:31:33,960 --> 01:31:36,640
I've told you, this one's called Pascal!

1060
01:31:36,820 --> 01:31:40,400
Once I deliver him to that owner,
everything will be completely settled!

1061
01:31:40,560 --> 01:31:45,480
It is impossible that its owner
would be tricked by this.

1062
01:31:45,660 --> 01:31:46,980
The main point is that
it has the same fur coat!

1063
01:31:47,120 --> 01:31:48,460
It's totally different!

1064
01:31:48,620 --> 01:31:51,040
-Mom! Dad!
-Ran.

1065
01:31:51,420 --> 01:31:53,640
Where on earth have you two been?

1066
01:31:53,840 --> 01:31:57,240
This absurdity of a man here said
he had to catch a raccoon...

1067
01:31:57,380 --> 01:32:00,460
So after searching the mountains
calling out, "Pascal, Pascal"...

1068
01:32:00,860 --> 01:32:03,500
In the end what he got was...

1069
01:32:03,660 --> 01:32:05,220
...this.

1070
01:32:05,760 --> 01:32:07,580
This is what you've been
doing all this time?

1071
01:32:08,000 --> 01:32:09,520
The entire time.

1072
01:32:09,660 --> 01:32:11,740
The main thing is
they're similar, right?

1073
01:32:12,700 --> 01:32:14,040
Ah, so itchy.

1074
01:32:14,220 --> 01:32:16,040
Still... Pascal turned out
to be a good tip.

1075
01:32:18,100 --> 01:32:21,760
Of course.
I knew that from the start.

1076
01:32:22,200 --> 01:32:24,000
That's why I kept on
telling you about Rascal.

1077
01:32:24,440 --> 01:32:28,180
-You should be thanking me.
-No, it's supposed to be "Pascal."

1078
01:32:37,740 --> 01:32:40,480
Wait! Don't leave me behind!

1079
01:32:40,620 --> 01:32:43,560
I thought I would help by
saying Rascal and Pascal.

1080
01:32:43,780 --> 01:32:46,040
Ah, he's running away.
Wait!

1081
01:32:46,820 --> 01:32:49,580
-! was surprised.
-Sorry.

1082
01:33:02,440 --> 01:33:05,480
There's always just one truth!

